140		This is not a separately named statement of the source article; it isolates the distribution equality in Lemma~\ref{lem:ld-question-typed-cl}. Fix $\mathsf{ldparams} = (q,m,d,k)$ as in Definition~\ref{def:ld-game}, let $L = \{L_t\}_{t \in \mathcal T^{\mathrm{ld}}}$ be the family of Definition~\ref{def:ld-question-distribution}, and let $G^{\mathrm{ld}}$ be the complete type graph. The question distribution of $\mathfrak G^{\mathrm{ld}}$ equals the distribution $\mu^{G^{\mathrm{ld}}}_{L,L}$ that the construction of Definition~\ref{def:typed-cl-distributions} produces from $(L,L)$ and $G^{\mathrm{ld}}$. This statement records only the distribution identity; Lemma~\ref{lem:ld-question-cl-family} supplies the common-level typed-family assertion.
141	\end{lemma}
142	\begin{proof}
143		\leanok
144		\uses{def:ld-question-distribution, def:typed-cl-distributions, def:graph-distribution, def:cl-dist, lem:distribution-map-comp, lem:uniform-bind-map}
